# Python / FastAPI Standards

## Async patterns
- Use async def for all database calls, HTTP calls, and WebSocket handlers
- Use asyncpg connection pools — never create new connections per request
- Background tasks use asyncio.create_task() or threading.Thread(daemon=True) with rationale

## FastAPI specifics
- All routes use Pydantic response_model=
- Use HTTPException with specific status codes
- Dependency injection for db pool, redis client, kronos engine, and dqg instance
- Router prefix structure: /api/v1/{resource}
- WebSocket endpoints in /ws/{channel}

## Error handling hierarchy
1. Catch specific exceptions first (asyncpg.PostgresError, redis.RedisError)
2. Log with context in structured form
3. Never swallow exceptions silently
4. DQG failures raise DQGFailureError — never silently return empty predictions

## Performance
- Use asyncpg executemany() for bulk inserts, never loop execute()
- Use TimescaleDB continuous aggregates for resampled reads
- Log Redis cache hit/miss at DEBUG level
